  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m focused on nailing down the application\'s core scope, specifically for the MCRA Solutions project. The provided specifications are my current touchstone. I\'m prioritizing the visual and functional consistency across the application screens, aiming to faithfully represent the provided screenshots and HTML specifications. It is important to me that I understand the design of the program.\n\n\n**Interpreting the Visuals**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the visual specifications. I am meticulously deconstructing the provided images to identify the core components. I\'m taking notes on the elements and their relationships within the design. Specifically, I am noting the use of 3D elements, the telemetry visualizations, the layout of the navigation drawers, and key performance indicators. The \"Panel Admin Socios\" screen is providing some useful insights into the functional requirements. I am considering the implications of the desktop vs. mobile views.\n\n\n**Analyzing Security Architecture**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the secure architecture elements. My mind\'s eye is visualizing the wireframe topology, and the technology stack: Python, Supabase, React/Next.js, and Kali Linux. I\'m considering Shamir\'s Secret Sharing for quorum topology. I am thinking through the implementation of immutable cryptographic contracts and the implications of the \"B\303\272nker de Silicio Cifrado\" photo callout. Also, I am taking into account the \"Client Alpha-1 Access Portal\" handshake and token verification. I\'m keeping Tier-1 zero breaches metrics in mind and what the implications of the cookie/telemetry banner are. I\'m now studying Image 7 and its display for desktop, specifically the sidebar navigation, top session header, and KPI tiles.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1848465"
