  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Design Tokens**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the color tokens specifically. The user\'s design is using several shades of blue and purple for surfaces. It seems the design might use different levels of contrast within a dark theme. I\'m focusing on the relationship between \"surface\" colors and their variations right now.\n\n\n**Examining Color Relationships**\n\nI\'ve been looking closely at the color tokens provided. I\'m noting the clear hierarchy among \"surface\" variations: `surface-container`, `surface-container-high`, and `surface-container-highest`. I\'m also seeing their corresponding text colors, such as `on-surface` and `on-surface-variant`. The design appears to be intentionally leveraging contrast for a distinct visual experience. I\'m focusing on how `inverse-surface` and `inverse-on-surface` fit into this picture, too.\n\n\n**Identifying Font and Icon Usage**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the typefaces in use. I\'ve noted Space Grotesk for `font-headline-sm` and Inter across multiple body sizes, with JetBrains Mono for code and labels. I see Material Symbols Outlined icons loaded as well. Now, I\'m setting my sights on the UI screens and features outlined in the request.\n\n\n**Reviewing Tech Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the live telemetry grid\'s performance metrics: operations per second, failover latency, and the certifications held. The architecture, specifically the shielded stack, is next: looking at the hardware root-of-trust, cryptographic algorithms, and auditing nodes. I\'m also assessing the tech stack carousel, noting each component, before examining security protocols.\n\n\n**Assessing Security Features**\n\nI\'m now examining the \"Client Alpha-1 Access Portal,\" specifically its Zero Trust Gateway with the pending TCP handshake. I see a need to focus on its restricted nature: corporate identifier input, security enclave key input, and the interactive WebAuthn simulation button for \"Verificar Token Hardware.\" I\'m also assessing the audit metrics with emphasis on \"Cero Brechas Hist\303\263ricas\" and \"Local-First Soberan\303\255a de Datos.\" I\'m reviewing the persistent cookie and cryptographic telemetry consent banner design with all options: \"Aceptar Todas\", \"Solo Esenciales\", and \"Preferencias Criptogr\303\241ficas\". Finally, I\'ve noted the scroll-to-top and scroll-to-bottom features.\n\n\n**Exploring Navigation Flows**\n\nI\'m now mapping out the user interfaces. I\'m focusing on the navigation, particularly the interaction between the mobile drawer and bottom bar. I\'ve taken a look at \"SISTEMA MCRA\" and its quick nav. I\'ve also noted how easily users can transition between public and admin sections via navigation bars or the mobile drawer in both the desktop enclave and mobile stack. The Executive Governance HUD with its cryptographic and admin session details also caught my attention.\n\n\n**Evaluating Security Credentials**\n\nI\'m now examining the \"RE-AUTH SESI\303\223N\" button, which triggers a credential validation modal using GitHub SSO, Supabase FIDO2, and an ECDSA session hash. Next I\'m assessing the KPI Bento Grid, especially the animated SVG sparkline showing monthly net gains. I\'m also reviewing the split bar visualizing dual fund dispersal and the lead generation metrics. I\'ll need to analyze the security scan results and the audited ledger table.\n\n\n**Analyzing Transaction Ledger**\n\nI\'m now diving into the transaction data and ledger entries. I\'ve noted the specifics: individual amounts, payment methods (SPEI, Stripe), and associated hashes. I\'m focusing on \"Grupo Inmobiliario Cero,\" \"Quantum Health B2B\" and \"Retail Enterprise MX\" and how they are recorded and verified. I\'m also planning to inspect the \"Nuevo Ticket\" modal and the live Kali daemon.\n\n\n"
